# Machine Wire Protocol & Diagnostics
File: openOODA/docs/spec/07_machine_wire.oot

This module defines the normative TSV diagnostic protocol, token dump wire
stream, process exit code matrix, and blackbox crash autopsy schema.

## 1. TSV Diagnostic Protocol

All openOODA tools emit machine-readable diagnostics in Tab-Separated Values:

### 1.1 Success Format
```tsv
OK\t<verb>\t<message>
```
- verb: Operation completed (e.g. build, check, test, loc, header, suite).
- message: Succinct status description.
- Example: OK\tcheck\toodac/main.oo clean
- Example: OK\tloc\topenOODA/spec.oot lines=168 (<= 256)

### 1.2 Error Format
```tsv
ERR\t<category>\t<message>
```
- Exactly two tab characters and three non-empty fields per line.
- category: Standardized failure category.
- Standard categories:
  - lex: Lexer error (unexpected byte, invalid float format, invalid BOM).
  - parse: Syntax error (missing semicolon, condition parentheses, commas).
  - type: Type error (type mismatch, missing match arm, unused Result/Option).
  - cap: Capability security violation (missing &Cap token, bad attenuation).
  - contract: Precondition or postcondition violation.
  - import: Cyclic import or unresolved module path.
  - env: Missing or malformed environment variables.
  - fs: File I/O access failure or path resolution error.
  - loc: File exceeds 256-line ceiling.
  - header: Malformed Academy or Clean header.
  - bit_parity: Token or capability bitmask mismatch.
  - determinism: Non-deterministic dual-run discrepancy.
  - suite: Aggregated test suite failure.

## 2. Token Dump Protocol

The compiler emits serialized token streams via "oodac tokens <file.oo>":

### 2.1 Wire Format
```tsv
<KIND>\t<LINE>\t<COL>\t<TEXT>
```
- KIND: Token identifier kind (e.g. IDENT, KW_FN, PLUS, INT).
- LINE: 1-indexed source line number.
- COL: 1-indexed source column number.
- TEXT: Verbatim source text for the token.

### 2.2 End-of-Stream Marker
The token stream terminates with a single EOF record:
```tsv
EOF\t<line>\t<col>\t
```

### 2.3 Escape Character Rules
In the TEXT column, special characters must be escaped:
- Tab (0x09) is escaped as \t.
- Line Feed (0x0A) is escaped as \n.
- Carriage Return (0x0D) is escaped as \r.
- Backslash (0x5C) is escaped as \\.

## 3. Process Exit Code Matrix (0..3)

Command-line tools in openOODA return standardized exit status codes:

| Code | Status               | Description                                    |
|------|----------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| 0    | Success              | Operation succeeded; all checks and tests pass |
| 1    | Execution Failure    | Test assertion failed, contract trap, or abort |
| 2    | Invocation Error     | CLI syntax error, invalid arguments, or parse  |
| 3    | Capability Violation | E_CAP security trap or Landlock sandbox breach |

Uncaught POSIX signals or fatal crashes preserve standard kernel codes (e.g.
128 + signal, such as 139 for SIGSEGV).

## 4. Blackbox Crash Autopsy JSON Schema

Under RFC 0007, unrecoverable crashes trigger the flight recorder:
- Async-signal-safe: Writes directly via Linux write() with zero heap memory.
- Target destination: .blackbox/autopsy.json.

### 4.1 Autopsy JSON Schema
```json
{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "timestamp": "2026-09-17T18:30:00Z",
  "failure_category": "SEGV_MAPERR",
  "signal": 11,
  "coordinate": {
    "file": "emit/llvm/ll_emit.oo",
    "line": 142,
    "col": 8
  },
  "stack_trace": [
    "oo_crash_handler",
    "ll_emit_function",
    "main"
  ],
  "flight_events": [
    { "seq": 104, "event": "ast_parse_complete" },
    { "seq": 105, "event": "llvm_lowering_start" }
  ],
  "root_cause": "Null pointer dereference in unmanaged foreign frame",
  "remediation": "Verify caller null check before invoking foreign function"
}
```
